    "file": "src/utils/body.ts",
    "line": 126,
    "summary": "parseBody on a HonoRequest now keeps the whole raw ArrayBuffer (`bodyCache.arrayBuffer`) and the parsed FormData (`bodyCache.formData`) alive for the rest of the request, where it used to keep only the FormData.",
    "failure_scenario": "A 100 MB multipart file upload parsed with `c.req.parseBody()` now holds about 200 MB (raw buffer plus File blobs) until the request ends, roughly doubling peak memory on upload endpoints compared with main."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/validator/validator.ts",
    "line": 24,
    "summary": "parseBody and validator now normalize Content-Type differently. parseBody splits on ';', trims and lowercases, but the validator regexes (now with /i) still don't allow whitespace before ';', and multipartRegex allows only a single `boundary` parameter.",
    "failure_scenario": "`Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded ; charset=UTF-8` is parsed by `c.req.parseBody()` but skipped by `validator('form')`, so the validator gets `{}`. `Multipart/Form-Data; charset=utf-8; boundary=abc` is also skipped by validator('form') even though parseBody accepts it. The same header gives different results depending on the API used."
  },
  {
    "file": "src/utils/buffer.ts",
    "line": 113,
    "summary": "Media-type normalization is now written three different ways: `split(';')[0].trim().toLowerCase()` in body.ts, `replace(/^[^;]+/, lower)` in buffer.ts, and `/i` regex flags in validator.ts. There is no shared helper.",
    "failure_scenario": "Maintenance cost and drift: the three versions already disagree on whitespace (body.ts trims, the validator regexes don't). A single `getMediaType(contentType)` helper in src/utils used by both parseBody and validator would keep them consistent."
